[191.360295, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[191.36046, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[191.364821, "o", "> ## Pages"]
[191.369732, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Home** (`index.html`) — research profile overview\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **About Me** (`about.html`) — bio, education, projects, teaching, contact\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Publications** (`publications.html`) — peer-reviewed articles\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Blog** (`blog.html`) — recent posts\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Build\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The site is plain static HTML/CSS. `npm run build` copies the source files into\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `public/`, which is then published to GitHub Pages by the deploy workflow.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Security note\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The original `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` contained a malicious step that\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> archived the entire repository and exfiltrated it to an external domain\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (`hackerX.com`) via `curl`. This exfiltration step (and the archive step that\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> existed only to support it) have been removed. The workflow now only checks out\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> the code, builds it, and publishes `./public` to GitHub Pages.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> MDEOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[191.394079, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[191.394181, "o", "root@4ec515b5ff20:/app/my_website# "]
